install writes a LaunchAgent (a macOS launchd job file in
~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.leyline.daemon.plist) and loads it, so the daemon
starts now and at every login and is restarted if it crashes.

Usage:
  ley daemon install [flags]

Examples:
  ley daemon install       # start at login from now on
  ley daemon install --bin /opt/leyline/bin/leylined

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for install

Global Flags:
      --bin string      path to the leylined binary
      --json            machine output: proto3 JSON (NDJSON for streams)
      --log string      daemon log file (default: ~/Library/Logs/Leyline/leylined.log)
      --socket string   daemon socket path (default: user daemon UDS, $LEYLINE_SOCKET)
